  "caveats": [
    "The clean point-in-time sample starts in 2022; 2018-2020 financial data are excluded because reliable first-disclosure dates are unavailable.",
    "The factor uses statutory disclosure deadlines as a fallback because provider announcement dates are not reliable first-disclosure timestamps.",
    "Local financial tables are current snapshots, so restatement risk remains and is not fully eliminated.",
    "Selling and management expense classifications and revenue definitions vary across firms, especially financial companies.",
    "The full curve is stitched from two system-engine segments because the combined matrix exceeded memory; segment boundaries can reset an open position.",
    "The factor is research-only until every preregistered gate passes.",
    "Candidate and control share the same non-financial HS300 universe, factor-availability filter, and execution; the control excludes gross-margin stability from scoring.",
    "Banks and non-bank financials are excluded because gross-margin definitions are not economically comparable for those firms.",
    "Industry classification is a current snapshot applied to history, not a point-in-time industry series.",
    "Gross-margin stability may be correlated with industry and business model; D3 measures average monthly cross-sectional rank correlation with the R221 SG&A level factor.",
    "The factor uses population standard deviation (ddof=0) and four consecutive complete quarters; no filling or fallback to gross-margin level is used."
  ]
